<title>RUSSIA: Russia Jan-May non-CIS nickel exports jump yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Russia Jan-May non-CIS nickel exports jump yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia exported 80,000 tonnes of nickel to countries outside the Commonwealth of Independent States in the first five months of 1997, 26 percent higher than the 63,500 tonnes in the same year-ago period, the State Statistics Committee said on Friday.</p>
<p>The committee, quoted by Interfax news agency, also said primary aluminium exports nudged down to 1.08 million tonnes in January-May, 0.4 percent down on the same year-ago levels.  </p>
<p>Russia exported 207,400 tonnes of copper to non-CIS destinations in January-May, 3.8 percent down on year-ago levels.</p>
<p>The committee gave the following data for Russian metal exports-</p>
<p>RUSSIAN JAN-MAY 1997 NON-CIS BASE METAL EXPORTS (TONNES)</p>
<p>			     Jan-May	 Jan-May	 pct</p>
<p>				1997	    1996	  change</p>
<p>								   yr/yr</p>
<p> Primary aluminium    1,080,700    1,085,100	 -0.4</p>
<p> Copper		     207,400	215,700	 -3.8</p>
<p> Nickel			80,000	 63,500	+26.0</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom +7095 941 8520</p>
